              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Barbara Myers Bakker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great lite dessert! As you can see from the photo I added, you can dress it up for a very festive display!",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-24T10:35:19.990Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GoodFoodLover"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Light and easy! My mother also made a dessert like this back in the 50s, but I never knew how she did it. Thanks for the recipe! Hers was lemon-flavored, a bit sweeter and she poured it over a wafer cookie crust. I made it with lime jello and added 2 T. Key Lime juice. Omitted the crumbs and served it as a chiffon. Wow, intense! Didn't take much to satisfy the taste buds. Will be serving this in the summer!",
            "datePublished": "2009-04-13T22:29:42.290Z"
          }
